{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791620162,"nonce":"MX+esz2wnZUTi8vbEVdPPRp77q8=","title":"The SSA builder copies every value's use set for a check that reads one table","message":"build_from_typed_cfg ended with build_def_use_chains, which cloned every value's `uses` set into SsaForm.def_use_chains and built use_def_chains beside it. Nothing reads def_use_chains; use_def_chains is read once, by SsaForm::verify, right after the build. build_def_use_chains was 4.4% of lower_program in a Lua nbody start-up profile. The builder's own sets of processed and reachable blocks, verify's set of defined values and HirFunction::rebuild_cfg_edges's predecessor map were SipHash-hashed.\n\nFix: SsaForm drops both chains; verify builds the one table it reads (each use to the last value naming it, as before, insertion-ordered); those sets and the predecessor map are Fx-hashed.\n\nStart-up instructions (llvm-backend build, PROFILE_STARTUP=10, median of 3, Mac): Python 9 kernels 47.76G -\u003e 46.87G (-1.85%; every kernel -1.3 to -2.3%); Lua 17 benchmarks 24.68G -\u003e 24.33G (-1.4%); output unchanged.","files":null}]}